  - agent skills
abstract: >-
  Session-Typed Skills (STJP) is a static compiler that type-checks the
  coordination protocol of a multi-agent LLM system before any agent runs. A
  natural-language intent is drafted into a multiparty session type, validated
  by the Scribble compiler for deadlock-freedom, communication safety, and
  goal reachability, and then statically projected into one interaction-safe
  local contract per agent plus a runtime enforcement monitor, value-dependent
  branch guards, and an execution scheduler derived from the same proof. The
  compiled code enforces the protocol on free-running, untrusted LLM agents at
  the message boundary. Benchmarked on real Azure AI Foundry agents, it catches
  deadlocks no runtime approach can, prevents unauthorized irreversible
  actions, and cuts agent calls and token cost by removing idle-agent polling.
